#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:1
msgid "ROS 2 Integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:3
msgid ""
"In this tutorial we will learn how to Integrate ROS 2 with Gazebo. We will "
"establish communication between them. This can help in many aspects; we can "
"receive data (like joint states, TFs) or commands from ROS and apply it to "
"Gazebo and vice versa. This can also help to enable RViz to visualize a "
"robot model simultaneously simulated by a Gazebo world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:8
msgid "ros_gz_bridge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:10
msgid ""
"[`ros_gz_bridge`](https://github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz) provides a network "
"bridge which enables the exchange of messages between ROS 2 and [Gazebo "
"Transport](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-transport). Its support is "
"limited to only certain message types. Please, check this [README](https://"
"github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz/blob/ros2/ros_gz_bridge/README.md) to verify if "
"your message type is supported by the bridge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:12
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:14
msgid ""
"Please follow the [Install Gazebo and ROS document](ros_installation) before "
"starting this tutorial. A working installation of ROS 2 and Gazebo is "
"required to go further."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:18
msgid "Bidirectional communication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:20
msgid ""
"We can initialize a bidirectional bridge so we can have ROS as the publisher "
"and Gazebo as the subscriber or vice versa."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:22
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:24
msgid "ros2 run ros_gz_bridge parameter_bridge /TOPIC@ROS_MSG@GZ_MSG\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:28
msgid ""
"The `ros2 run ros_gz_bridge parameter_bridge` command simply runs the "
"`parameter_bridge` code from the `ros_gz_bridge` package. Then, we specify "
"our topic `/TOPIC` over which the messages will be sent. The first `@` "
"symbol delimits the topic name from the message types. Following the first "
"`@` symbol is the ROS message type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:30
msgid "The ROS message type is followed by an `@`, `[`, or `]` symbol where:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:32
msgid "`@`  is a bidirectional bridge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:33
msgid "`[`  is a bridge from Gazebo to ROS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:34
msgid "`]`  is a bridge from ROS to Gazebo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:36
msgid ""
"Have a look at these [examples]( https://github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz/blob/"
"ros2/ros_gz_bridge/README.md#example-1a-gazebo-transport-talker-and-ros-2-"
"listener) explaining how to make communication connections from ROS to "
"Gazebo and vice versa."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:39
msgid "Publish key strokes to ROS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:41
msgid "Let's send messages to ROS using the `Key Publisher` an Gazebo plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:43
msgid ""
"**Note:** Make sure to have all workspaces you need (ROS, Gazebo and, "
"`ros_gz`...) sourced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:46
msgid ""
"First we will start a bridge between ROS and Gazebo specifying the topic at "
"which the `Key Publisher` plugin sends messages and also the type of the "
"messages as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:50
msgid ""
"ros2 run ros_gz_bridge parameter_bridge /keyboard/keypress@std_msgs/msg/"
"Int32@gz.msgs.Int32\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:54
msgid ""
"We started a bridge on `/keyboard/keypress` topic with message of type "
"`Int32`. For ROS it is `std_msgs/msg/Int32` and for Gazebo it is `gz.msgs."
"Int32`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:57
msgid ""
"In another terminal launch an Gazebo Sim world, for example the `empty.sdf` "
"world:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:59
msgid "gz sim empty.sdf\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:63
msgid ""
"Then add the `Key Publisher` plugin from the dropdown menu on the top right "
"corner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:65
msgid ""
"![empty_world_with_KeyPublisher](tutorials/ros2_integration/empty_world.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:65
msgid "empty_world_with_KeyPublisher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:67
msgid "In another terminal start the ROS listener:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:69
msgid "ros2 topic echo /keyboard/keypress\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:73
msgid ""
"This command listens to the messages sent over the `/keyboard/keypress` "
"topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:75
msgid ""
"On the Gazebo window, press on the keyboard keys and you should find data on "
"the listener terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:78
msgid ""
"Now it's your turn! Try to send data from ROS to Gazebo. You can also try "
"different data types and different directions of communication."
msgstr ""

