#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:86
msgid "Visualize in RViz"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:88
msgid ""
"Take a step further and try out demos from [`ros_gz_sim_demos`](https://"
"github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz/tree/ros2/ros_gz_sim_demos)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:90
msgid ""
"For the `sdf_parser` demo, install [`ros_gz`](https://github.com/gazebosim/"
"ros_gz/tree/ros2) and the parser plugin `sdformat_urdf` from source in a "
"colcon workspace. Read more about `sdformat_urdf` [here](https://github.com/"
"ros/sdformat_urdf/blob/ros2/sdformat_urdf/README.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:93
msgid "Run the demo launch file with the rviz launch argument set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:95
msgid "ros2 launch ros_gz_sim_demos sdf_parser.launch.py rviz:=True\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:99
msgid ""
"Start the simulation in Gazebo and wait a few seconds for TFs to be "
"published."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:101
msgid ""
"In another terminal, send either ROS or Gazebo commands for the vehicle to "
"move in circles:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:103
msgid ""
"gz topic -t \"/model/vehicle/cmd_vel\" -m gz.msgs.Twist -p \"linear: {x: "
"1.0}, angular: {z: -0.1}\"\n"
"ros2 topic pub /model/vehicle/cmd_vel geometry_msgs/msg/Twist \"{linear: {x: "
"5.0, y: 0.0, z: 0.0}, angular: {x: 0.0, y: 0.0, z: -0.1}}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:108
msgid "And verify the vehicle matching its trajectory in Gazebo and RViz."
msgstr ""

